  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🎩 Funny Wizard Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Wizards who take themselves far too seriously: Gloop the Magnificent, Fizzledorf Thunderpants, Noodlecrack the Wise."
    },
    "intro": "The funniest wizard names sound grand for about half a second. This **funny wizard name generator** has hundreds of them, with a title the wizard gave themselves (<em>Gloop the Magnificent</em>) or a surname they'd rather you didn't mention (<em>Fizzledorf Thunderpants</em>). Good for comic fantasy, parodies, and the party wizard who keeps setting things on fire.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The great comic wizards",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Rincewind</strong>, Terry Pratchett's cowardly wizard, can't spell his own job: his hat says WIZZARD. The Unseen University's staff include Archchancellor Mustrum Ridcully, the Bursar and Ponder Stibbons, all names that sound like they belong in a dusty common room.</li><li><strong>Tim the Enchanter</strong>, in <em>Monty Python and the Holy Grail</em>, is funny because his name is so ordinary.</li><li><strong>Dumbledore</strong> was a joke too: J. K. Rowling has said it's an old word for a bumblebee, chosen because she imagined him humming to himself.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "What makes a wizard name funny",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Silly sounds</strong>: lots of <em>z</em>, <em>wobble</em>, <em>fizzle</em> and <em>-wick</em>. Say it out loud and it should sound slightly wrong.</li><li><strong>A grand title that doesn't fit</strong>: <em>the Magnificent</em>, <em>the Wise</em>, <em>the Eternal</em>, on someone called Noodlecrack.</li><li><strong>An honest one</strong>: <em>the Forgetful</em>, <em>the Half-Baked</em>, <em>the Bewildered</em>.</li><li><strong>A surname from the laundry</strong>: Thunderpants, Puddlewhisker, Gloomspoon.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Using a funny wizard",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Comic relief in a serious game</strong>: a wizard called Boffle the Bewildered can say things a grim hero can't.</li><li><strong>A whole silly campaign</strong>: give every wizard in the tower a name from here and let the players work out who's actually competent.</li><li><strong>Need a straight one?</strong> Try the <a href=\"wizard-name-generator.html\">Wizard Name Generator</a>.</li></ul>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "Are these names family-friendly?",
